<h2>The rebrand and relaunch</h2>
<p>In November 2026 the archive returned as ArtCard.LA, the name already used for the cards. It is a new home for the same collection — {{ groups.stats.artworks }} ArtCards published on LA-Artist.com between {{ groups.stats.first | niceDate }} and {{ groups.stats.last | niceDate }}. You will still see LA-Artist.com on the original cards, in the books, and in earlier exhibitions. Follow the archive on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/artcard.la/">Instagram</a>.</p>
<h2>About this archive</h2>
<p>Each card is listed under the artist name and ZIP code written on it, as recorded on the original site. Cards without a usable ZIP code are grouped under <a href="{{ '/region/outside-la/' | url }}">Outside LA / California</a>, <a href="{{ '/region/us-states/' | url }}">U.S. States</a>, <a href="{{ '/region/international/' | url }}">International</a> and <a href="{{ '/region/unknown/' | url }}">Unknown</a>. Images are shown at the size they were originally published. All artworks remain © their artists.</p>
<h2>Map data</h2>
<p>ZIP code boundaries: County of Los Angeles Enterprise GIS, “Zipcodes” layer (Administrative Boundaries), accessed November 2026 and simplified for the web, used under the <a href="https://egis-lacounty.hub.arcgis.com/pages/terms-of-use">LA County GIS Data Portal Terms of Use</a>. This use does not imply endorsement by the County of Los Angeles. Base map tiles © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors. Map built with <a href="https://leafletjs.com">Leaflet</a>.</p>
